so there is devastating just devastating  new evidence in the Trump Ukraine  quid-pro-quo Fiasco and it is really  important to understand what we mean by  evidence and I think this is really  worth doing so I'm gonna focus on that  element today and I hope that this is  useful there is new testimony under oath  from the United States envoy to the  Ukraine who says that listen the story  we've been getting publicly is true  Donald Trump indeed made the security  aid hundreds of millions of dollars in  security aid to Ukraine contingent on  dependent upon Ukraine publicly saying  that they were going to carry out this  politically motivated smear  investigation against Joe and hunter  Biden that is as a fact not very  surprising to people in my audience I  presume who have been following the  story but this is the really important  part that I want to focus on today if we  go back to the Russia probe and carry  through to what is going on now with  Ukraine and the impeachment inquiry the  Trump is right has insisted time and  time again that there is no evidence  that everything that there is in the  Trump Russia probe with the Ukraine  Fiasco it is hearsay and people's  baseless allegations and this is why we  have to be just super crystal clear here  because unless we are prepared to  address this farcical claim they're  going to get away with it okay testimony  under oath is evidence now there is a  difference between evidence and sort of  caught red-handed irrefutable proof but  before we even get to that we have to  understand how they are distorting what  actually counts as evidence and before I  go into this let me give you an analogy  which i think is useful here consider  the word theory okay the word theory has  one meaning in colloquial usage and it  has another meaning in the world of  science in science when the when the  term theory is used we're talking about  a group of propositions that explain  facts or explain some real-world  phenomena for example the theory of  evolution  that is a very specific meaning in the  world of science but the word theory in  popular culture in colloquial usage has  a different meaning and theory in  colloquial usage often actually means  what in science is called a hypothesis  which is it's sort of like a starting  point or it's a possibility it's one of  many possibilities for explaining  something in the real world and one of  the things that the American right-wing  loves to do is for example in the  context of climate change deliberately  miss state or flip between definitions  of what they mean by theory they'll just  deliberately distort the definition of  theory by switching back and forth  between the scientific definition and  the colloquial usage which really means  hypothesis they'll say you know a theory  about climate change a theory is just  one of 20 30 or 40 different  explanations about what's going on well  hold on a second that may be what it  means in colloquial usage but when  science call something a theory it has a  different meaning now let's go back to  this evidence thing bearing in mind this  analogy from you know theory hypothesis  all along Republicans have said there is  no evidence for anything in the Russia  probe there is no evidence of any quid  pro quo in the Ukraine Fiasco sometimes  they'll also use the word hearsay  they'll say it's all hearsay what they  mean is no one has been caught on video  in a cartoonish out of the movies sort  of red-handed way that satisfies them as  irrefutable proof but here's the really  important thing sworn testimony is  evidence William Taylor the United  States envoy to Ukraine provided sworn  testimony to lawmakers where he says  there is no question that Donald Trump  was withholding aid in order to try to  get Ukraine to smear Joe Biden and  hunter Biden publicly so now the  trumpets are coming in and they're  saying hold on a second what William  Taylor says is not evidence it's merely  hearsay which is also the wrong word but  let's forget that for now we're not  gonna get into hearsay right now  sworn testimony is evidence sworn  testimony is evidence made under oath or  affirmation under penalty of perjury now  someone could give sworn testimony and  be lying someone could give sworn  testimony and not remember the facts  correctly but when the right says there  is no evidence that's either a lie or an  ignorant understanding of what evidence  means the testimony is evidence but  here's where the theory versus  hypothesis thing comes back to be useful  they're also using evidence  interchangeably with proof this is the  other game that they're playing William  Taylor giving evidence that Donald Trump  withheld aid in a quid pro quo for Joe  Biden to be smeared is not irrefutable  proof that that took place and that's  okay but what they are often saying when  they say there is no evidence is that it  is not a refutable proof which is a  completely different standard it's a  completely different issue  so now understanding this all of this  relates to the total and complete lack  of critical thinking and epistemology  skills in our society which I've been  sounding the alarm about for years at  this point when people understand how  arguments are made when people  understand how to figure out for  themselves if the words being used to  describe things are the most accurate  and precise words that could be used you  can't trick people like this the climate  change theory hypothesis games the games  around what counts as evidence versus  proof you can only get traction with  distortions and lies you can only  confuse people semantically when people  don't have the skills to think these  things through for themselves and that's  really the tragedy that's really the  saddest thing of all about the status  quo of American just ability to think  critically now some last thoughts about  the substance of the testimony from  William Taylor the US envoy to Ukraine  just to kind of come full circle and do  at least some small analysis of that  although it doesn't really warrant much  of an analysis because we know what's  going on number one the testimony is  truly devastating to the Trump narrative  because everyone involved who has given  testimony  including testimony about their  knowledge of that Trump phone call with  the Ukrainian president even Mick  Mulvaney without realizing it without  meaning to everyone is confirming  elements of the story that the aid was  contingent upon the smears of Joe Biden  now after the fact they'll deny it  they'll try to go back and again play  semantic games about the definitions of  the words that they used but that is the  trend  everybody's confirming the original  story even if they don't mean to  secondly this also seems to have  jump-started Fox News back into state  media mode where you know we've talked  about there have been recently some  disagreements between Fox News and  Donald Trump on some minor issues the  last 24 hours the testimony from William  Taylor has completely restarted Fox  News's narrative around the entire  Ukraine thing is a nothing burger it's  all a smear attempt against Donald Trump  it's all a witch-hunt etc they covered  this story about William Taylor's  testimony as if the testimony from  William Taylor is obviously not credible  and suggests that the Trump witch-hunt  narrative is the correct one which I  mean imagine being that disconnected  from reality that that's your takeaway  and again to go back to the conversation  between Donald Trump and the Ukrainian  president the excerpt that was released  they initially said it was a transcript  then they said well it's not a  transcript it's it's a summation in  reality it was a partial transcript  Trump released that believing that it  vindicated him anyone who again can  think for themselves can apply basic  critical thinking and epistemology  skills to a document and not be swayed  by the story that Donald Trump tells you  about it you realize that that partial  transcript is extraordinarily damning  when it comes to Donald Trump's  involvement in this quid pro quo we will  see what the future is of this entire  thing I know that there are people in  the audience who from a practical  perspective are saying listen David I  know you're right and it's not just you  that's saying I mean it's anybody who  analyzes the evidence understands what  it is that took place here but it is  going to be hard to get Trump on it and  I don't disagree with you and that's why  all of these in  negations all of these discussions they  need to be properly contextualized in  let's use them to motivate voters to go  out and vote for someone other than  Donald Trump because the most likely  scenario I know that there are other  paths the most likely scenario is none  of this stuff will forcefully remove  Trump from office but if we play it  correctly if we talk about it in the  right way it will motivate voters to go  out on November of whatever the data is  early November 2020 and say no more I'm  voting for somebody else let me know  what you think I'm on Twitter at D  Pakman the show is on Twitter at David  Pakman show
 

